WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:05.214
Ally froze.

2
00:00:05.215 --> 00:00:11.005
The new customers were the mother and little girl who'd spotted her at the park right after her landing.

3
00:00:11.006 --> 00:00:16.251
"I'm not an alien!" Ally blurted. "It's your word against mine!"

4
00:00:16.252 --> 00:00:19.740
The mother looked confused.

5
00:00:19.741 --> 00:00:22.922
"I mean . . ." Ally tried to laugh it off.

6
00:00:22.923 --> 00:00:32.603
"Just kidding. Beep-beep! Boop!" She made a few strange sounds. "Okay, I'm an alien!"

7
00:00:32.604 --> 00:00:39.153
The little girl laughed at Ally's funny alien imitation.

8
00:00:39.154 --> 00:00:42.847
"See, Mommy! I told you she was an alien.

9
00:00:42.848 --> 00:00:46.955
Can we bring Grandpa Lloyd here so he can see her too?"

10
00:00:46.956 --> 00:00:51.260
"Come along, honey," the mother said as she led her daughter out of the diner.

11
00:00:51.261 --> 00:00:56.087
"We'll be late for Grandpa's lecture."

12
00:00:56.088 --> 00:01:01.189
They were finally gone, but Ally could still feel her heart pounding in her chest.

13
00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:09.593
She went over to the counter to refill some salt shakers, but she was so rattled, she spilled salt all over the place.

14
00:01:09.594 --> 00:01:12.829
She was cleaning it up when Ray called from the kitchen.

15
00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:18.904
"Ally!" He sounded mad. "I need to speak with you."

16
00:01:18.905 --> 00:01:25.434
"Oh no! What now?" she thought, going into the kitchen.

17
00:01:25.435 --> 00:01:29.568
"I think it's time you found a new job," Ray said sternly.

18
00:01:29.569 --> 00:01:32.527
Ally's eyes filled with tears.

19
00:01:32.528 --> 00:01:37.582
"Is it because of what the little girl said? I promise you, I'm not what you think, Ray.

20
00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:45.343
I mean, I am, but I was only trying to do good deeds and restore peaceful balance here!"

21
00:01:45.344 --> 00:01:50.064
Ray scratched his head. "What?"

22
00:01:50.065 --> 00:01:55.838
"Never mind. Why do I have to leave?" Ally asked.

23
00:01:55.839 --> 00:02:01.782
"I can't afford to keep the diner open any longer," Ray explained. "I'm shutting down."

24
00:02:01.783 --> 00:02:09.213
"But we were so busy today. You can't give up now, Ray!"

25
00:02:09.214 --> 00:02:11.770
"One good day isn't going to save me, Ally. I—"

26
00:02:11.771 --> 00:02:14.680
"Oh my gosh!" Kate cried.

27
00:02:14.681 --> 00:02:18.397
Ally and Ray raced into the dining room.

28
00:02:18.398 --> 00:02:20.841
"What's wrong?" Ray cried.

29
00:02:20.842 --> 00:02:26.045
Kate looked up from her phone. "Have you ever heard of Gourmet Greta?"

30
00:02:26.046 --> 00:02:28.387
"No," Ray said.

31
00:02:28.388 --> 00:02:31.205
"Well, she's the hottest food blogger there is.

32
00:02:31.206 --> 00:02:33.654
I follow her on all my socials.

33
00:02:33.655 --> 00:02:38.030
A review from Gourmet Greta can make or break a restaurant."

34
00:02:38.031 --> 00:02:44.345
"A big-time restaurant critic is never going to come to Sandville to review a diner," Ray said.

35
00:02:44.346 --> 00:02:48.274
"She already has!" Kate said. "Look!"

36
00:02:48.275 --> 00:02:55.615
She held up her comm device to show them a posting: "Ray's Diner: Out of This World or Crashing Comet?"

37
00:02:55.616 --> 00:03:02.156
Bethany frowned. "I don't get it. Is that a good review or a bad one?"

38
00:03:02.157 --> 00:03:06.147
"Greta likes to keep the reader guessing until the last line of her review.

39
00:03:06.148 --> 00:03:10.350
She never gives away anything in the titles," Kate said.

40
00:03:10.351 --> 00:03:16.192
Worry knitted Ray's brow. "I don't think I want to hear this."

41
00:03:16.193 --> 00:03:21.344
Kate smiled. "Yes, you do." She read aloud.

42
00:03:21.345 --> 00:03:27.190
Ray's Diner, located near Sandville's famous UFO museum, is full of surprises.

43
00:03:27.191 --> 00:03:31.962
Though the decor is simple, there's nothing plain about the food or the service.

44
00:03:31.963 --> 00:03:37.189
Everything I ate there was delicious. And the service is unmatched.

45
00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:42.475
There's only one waitress, and she's sweet, funny, and always seems to have a surprise up her sleeve.

46
00:03:42.476 --> 00:03:50.524
Whether she's suggesting exactly the right dish to customers or performing entertaining tricks, she always adds to the fun.

47
00:03:50.525 --> 00:03:57.594
If you're looking for great food and hospitality, head to Ray's Diner. A+ rating.

48
00:03:57.595 --> 00:04:08.396
Mateo cheered. "You're a hit, Papi!"

49
00:04:08.397 --> 00:04:13.785
But Ally was confused. "I don't recall serving any restaurant critics."

50
00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:21.235
"Gourmet Greta dresses up in disguises so nobody knows she's reviewing the restaurant," Kate explained.

51
00:04:21.236 --> 00:04:27.669
"But she includes a photo in her reviews—it has hints of what she wore to the restaurant."

52
00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:30.254
Ally examined the photo in the review.

53
00:04:30.255 --> 00:04:36.064
"The hints are big eyeglasses, a cane, and a leopard-print dress.

54
00:04:36.065 --> 00:04:43.982
I served this woman three different times."

55
00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:48.325
"Wait, there's more." Bethany read from her own comm device.

56
00:04:48.326 --> 00:04:53.358
"'The only thing Ray's is missing to attract more customers is a theme.

57
00:04:53.359 --> 00:05:00.296
Ray, if you want Greta's advice, remember that you're the closest restaurant to the museum.

58
00:05:00.297 --> 00:05:05.777
So a UFO or space theme would be a perfect fit.'"

59
00:05:05.778 --> 00:05:08.885
"Awesome idea!" Mateo said.

60
00:05:08.886 --> 00:05:14.885
Ray lifted his eyebrows. "It might work . . ."

61
00:05:14.886 --> 00:05:18.933
"Can I help with new decorations?" Bethany asked.

62
00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:22.743
"Yes!" Mateo's cheeks turned red again.

63
00:05:22.744 --> 00:05:27.252
"I'll help too," Kate said. "I'm really good at shopping."

64
00:05:27.253 --> 00:05:30.923
"Let's get to work," Ray said.

65
00:05:30.924 --> 00:05:35.885
Ally stood back, watching as the others started planning the restaurant makeover.

66
00:05:35.886 --> 00:05:38.914
She was happy that Ray's Diner might be saved after all.

67
00:05:38.915 --> 00:05:42.215
But now she herself needed help.

68
00:05:42.216 --> 00:05:53.318
"If the little girl brings Dr. Cosmo Lloyd to the diner," Ally thought, "I'm in trouble—meteor-size trouble!"

